{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LymZ4mRr4zCGuL3HJy3pKu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Median 档预期：1-2 个审稿人对 CF 9.9%-12.02%、DocRED Qwen DR↓仅44.7%、novelty\n2\t  提出 major concern。 整体叙事不需重构，但需要：(1) title 加 qualifier (''under Single-Relation Scope'')；\n3\t  (2) Claim 1 tightness insight 从因果降级为 correlational；(3) §5 补充 Constraint Coverage\n4\t  ablation， 将 DocRED 弱效果转化为 ''predictable from coverage metric'' 的 positive finding；\n5\t  (4) 强化 §3 violation landscape 独立贡献 + decidability taxonomy formalism 回应 novelty\n6\t  质疑； (5) 增加 F1 regime sensitivity discussion。Rebuttal 工作量 7-14 天。 审稿人 profile：R1\n7\t  偏 systems/engineering（接受方法，质疑 CF）；R2 偏 NLP（质疑 novelty + DocRED 表现）； R3 中立偏正面（接受\n8\t  zero-shot framing，建议 expand cross-model）。\n9\t\n10\t  '\n11\timagined_experiments:\n12\t- name: SciERC violation rate (minimal prompt)\n13\t  plan_id: P001\n14\t  description: 'Qwen3-8B zero-shot SciERC extraction，minimal prompt，测量 baseline violation\n15\t    rates。 7 relations, 551 abstracts。\n16\t\n17\t    '\n18\t  expected_results:\n19\t    total_triples: 1724\n20\t    total_entities: 2474\n21\t    json_parse_rate: 1.0\n22\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.004\n23\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0139\n24\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1537\n25\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0008\n26\t    entity_f1: 0.3101\n27\t    relation_f1: 0.0823\n28\t    per_relation_dr_top3:\n29\t      Compare: 0.4242\n30\t      Feature-of: 0.3354\n31\t      Part-of: 0.25\n32\t    per_relation_dr_bottom2:\n33\t      Used-for: 0.0076\n34\t      Conjunction: 0.0\n35\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下，15.4% DR baseline 被 2/3 审稿人接受为 non-trivial。R2 可能质疑：\n36\t    \"zero-shot 本身就会产生各种错误，15% constraint violation 在 8% F1 下是否真的重要？\" 但 per-relation\n37\t    分布（Compare 42%、Used-for 0.8%）的极端差异足以说服—— 这不是随机错误，是 constraint tightness 相关的系统性现象。\n38\t    R1 接受此数据作为 motivation。R3 认为 violation landscape 是独立贡献。\n39\t\n40\t    '\n41\t  tables:\n42\t  - 'Table 1: Per-relation DR violation rates (SciERC, minimal prompt). 7 relations\n43\t    ranked by tightness τ.'\n44\t  figures_description:\n45\t  - 'Figure 2: Scatter plot of constraint tightness (τ = 1 - valid_pairs/total_pairs)\n46\t    vs. DR violation rate per relation type. Clear positive correlation (r=0.87) supporting\n47\t    Claim 1.'\n48\t  analysis: 'R2 在 median 档会写：\"The violation landscape analysis (§3) provides useful\n49\t    empirical grounding, but the causal claim that ''violation rate is driven by tightness''\n50\t    is overstated given confounds (relation frequency, entity type distribution).\"\n51\t    需在 rebuttal 中降级为 correlational + 补充 frequency 作为 covariate 的分析。\n52\t\n53\t    '\n54\t- name: SciERC violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\n55\t  plan_id: P002\n56\t  description: 'Qwen3-8B SciERC，schema-informed prompt 将 domain/range constraints\n57\t    写入 prompt， 测量 prompt-level intervention 效果。\n58\t\n59\t    '\n60\t  expected_results:\n61\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.0578\n62\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.003\n63\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n64\t    total_triples: 1661\n65\t    vs_minimal_dr_reduction_pct: -62.4\n66\t    per_relation_notable:\n67\t      Feature-of_delta_pp: -22.3\n68\t      Part-of_delta_pp: -22.5\n69\t      Compare_delta_pp: -14.8\n70\t      Evaluate-for_delta_pp: 5.8\n71\t    mcnemar_significant: true\n72\t  result_rationale: '62.4% reduction 在 median 档被全部审稿人接受为 \"substantial but insufficient\"。\n73\t    关键攻击面是 Evaluate-for 回归 (+5.8pp)：R2 会写 \"The fact that prompting can *increase*\n74\t    violations for specific relation types (Evaluate-for, §3.2) is an interesting\n75\t    finding but needs more analysis — is this a prior-constraint conflict or simply\n76\t    noise?\" Median 档下 R2 对此提出 minor weakness 而非 major，因为论文已有 prior-constraint conflict\n77\t    解释框架。但 R2 建议 \"run significance test on per-relation changes to distinguish real\n78\t    regression from variance.\"\n79\t\n80\t    '\n81\t  tables:\n82\t  - 'Table 2: Per-relation DR rates under minimal vs. schema-informed prompts, with\n83\t    McNemar test results.'\n84\t  figures_description: []\n85\t  analysis: 'Schema-informed prompt 数据在 median 档基本无争议，支撑 Claim 2。 Evaluate-for 回归是一个\n86\t    talking point 但不构成 major weakness。\n87\t\n88\t    '\n89\t- name: DocRED violation rate (minimal prompt)\n90\t  plan_id: P003\n91\t  description: 'Qwen3-8B DocRED (998 docs, 96 relations)，minimal prompt baseline。\n92\t\n93\t    '\n94\t  expected_results:\n95\t    total_docs: 998\n96\t    parsed_docs: 962\n97\t    json_parse_rate: 0.964\n98\t    total_entities: 19099\n99\t    total_triples: 16540\n100\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.075\n101\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.289\n102\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.187\n103\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0008\n104\t    top_dr_by_rate:\n105\t      P35_head_of_state: 1.0\n106\t      P710_participant: 0.919\n107\t      P172_ethnic_group: 0.875\n108\t    top_dr_by_count:\n109\t      P31_instance_of:\n110\t        violations: 322\n111\t        total: 533\n112\t        rate: 0.604\n113\t      P1001_applies_to_jurisdiction:\n114\t        violations: 264\n115\t        total: 594\n116\t        rate: 0.444\n117\t  result_rationale: 'DocRED 18.7% DR vs SciERC 15.4%——14× ontology size 差异下 violation\n118\t    rate 相近—— 直接支撑 \"violation rate driven by tightness not ontology size\" claim。 Median\n119\t    档下 R1 接受此 finding。R2 会注意到 RV=28.9% 极高，质疑： \"Nearly 30% of generated relation names\n120\t    are out-of-vocabulary — how much of DR is confounded by the model simply not knowing\n121\t    the relation names?\" 这是 D014 dual-factor insight 的前兆。R2 不会因此 reject 但会要求 disentangle\n122\t    RV 和 DR 的交互效应。\n123\t\n124\t    '\n125\t  tables:\n126\t  - 'Table 1 (extended): DocRED violation rates. Top-10 relations by DR rate and count.'\n127\t  figures_description:\n128\t  - 'Figure 2 (right panel): DocRED tightness vs. DR scatter, colored by relation\n129\t    frequency.'\n130\t  analysis: 'RV=28.9% 是 DocRED 特有现象（96 relations 中很多 Qwen 未见过）。 Median R2 会追问 \"如果先修\n131\t    RV 再测 DR，DR 会不会更低？\"——恰好引出 grammar_only 实验。\n132\t\n133\t    '\n134\t- name: DocRED violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\n135\t  plan_id: P004\n136\t  description: 'DocRED schema-informed prompt，测量 prompt-level 在复杂 ontology 上的效果。\n137\t\n138\t    '\n139\t  expected_results:\n140\t    total_documents: 998\n141\t    documents_checked: 943\n142\t    json_parse_rate: 0.9449\n143\t    total_triples: 16782\n144\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0061\n145\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.1841\n146\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1284\n147\t    vs_minimal_dr_reduction_pct: -31.3\n148\t  result_rationale: 'DR↓31.3% vs SciERC ↓62.4%——prompt intervention 在复杂 ontology 上效果减半。\n149\t    Median 档下所有审稿人接受此数据。R2 会标注 \"The scaling gap between SciERC (62%) and DocRED (31%)\n150\t    prompt-level reduction is compelling evidence for Claim 2, though confounded by\n151\t    the 96-relation prompt being much longer and potentially overwhelming the model''s\n152\t    attention.\" 这是 minor point，不构成 major weakness。 R1 认为此数据强化了 decoding-time 方法的 motivation。\n153\t\n154\t    '\n155\t  tables:\n156\t  - 'Table 2 (DocRED section): Schema-informed prompt results.'\n157\t  figures_description: []\n158\t  analysis: 'Prompt insufficiency claim (C2) 在 median 档获得 3/3 审稿人支持。 这是论文最安全的 claim——数据清晰，叙事直觉合理。\n159\t\n160\t    '\n161\t- name: SciERC unconstrained baseline\n162\t  plan_id: P005a\n163\t  description: 'Phase 2 SciERC unconstrained（与 Phase 0 同 pipeline 但 Phase 2 checker\n164\t    v2）， 作为 ablation 的 control condition。\n165\t\n166\t    '\n167\t  expected_results:\n168\t    total_samples: 551\n169\t    total_triples: 1724\n170\t    total_entities: 2474\n171\t    json_parse_rate: 1.0\n172\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.004\n173\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0139\n174\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1537\n175\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0008\n176\t    entity_f1: 0.3101\n177\t    relation_f1: 0.0823\n178\t  result_rationale: '与 P001 数值一致（同模型同数据同 prompt，仅 checker 版本更新后数值不变）。 Median 档下此实验本身无争议，仅作为\n179\t    ablation table 的 row 0。 R2 可能注意到 R-F1=8.23% 绝对值低，引出 C8 concern。\n180\t\n181\t    '\n182\t  tables:\n183\t  - 'Table 3 row 1: SciERC unconstrained baseline metrics.'\n184\t  figures_description: []\n185\t  analysis: 'Baseline 数据确保 ablation 有公平比较基准。F1=8.23% 的 low absolute value 在 median\n186\t    档下被 R2 提及一次（\"results are in very low F1 regime\"）但被 zero-shot framing 部分化解（R3 接受，R2\n187\t    remains skeptical）。\n188\t\n189\t    '\n190\t- name: SciERC grammar-only\n191\t  plan_id: P005\n192\t  description: '仅启用 grammar layer (XGrammar CFG)，验证 grammar 层对 violation 的独立效果。\n193\t\n194\t    '\n195\t  expected_results:\n196\t    total_triples: 1725\n197\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n198\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0\n199\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1484\n200\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0008\n201\t    entity_f1: 0.3098\n202\t    relation_f1: 0.0823\n203\t  result_rationale: 'Grammar 层消除 ET/RV（→0%）但 DR 几乎不变（15.37%→14.84%，Δ-0.53pp）—— 完美演示\n204\t    grammar 只管 vocabulary 不管 semantics。Median 档下 3/3 审稿人认为 此 ablation 清晰有效。R1 可能评价\n205\t    \"The ablation clearly demonstrates the orthogonal contributions of the two layers\n206\t    — grammar handles vocabulary, semantic handles domain/range.\" CF=0.08% 也证明 grammar\n207\t    层不引入 CF——CF 100% 来自 semantic 层。\n208\t\n209\t    '\n210\t  tables:\n211\t  - 'Table 3 row 2: SciERC grammar-only.'\n212\t  figures_description: []\n213\t  analysis: 'Grammar-only 是 enabling dependency 叙事的关键证据。DR 不降说明 grammar 是 semantic\n214\t    的 prerequisite 而非 replacement。\n215\t\n216\t    '\n217\t- name: SciERC semantic-only\n218\t  plan_id: P006\n219\t  description: '仅启用 semantic layer (TypeConstraintProcessor)，无 grammar 保底。\n220\t\n221\t    '\n222\t  expected_results:\n223\t    total_triples: 1726\n224\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.004\n225\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0151\n226\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1165\n227\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0271\n228\t    entity_f1: 0.3101\n229\t    relation_f1: 0.0815\n230\t  result_rationale: 'Semantic-only DR↓24%（vs full_s1 ↓94%）——没有 grammar 保底时 semantic\n231\t    层遇到 OOV relation types 无法 enforce constraints，效果大打折扣。RV=1.51% 残余证明 semantic 不管\n232\t    vocabulary。Median 档下此数据被 R1 引用为 \"convincing evidence for the enabling dependency\n233\t    between layers.\" R2 同意但追问 \"What fraction of the 76% gap (24% vs 94%) is due to\n234\t    OOV vs. other failure modes?\" 需 rebuttal 补充 OOV relation 占 semantic failure 的比例分析。\n235\t\n236\t    '\n237\t  tables:\n238\t  - 'Table 3 row 3: SciERC semantic-only.'\n239\t  figures_description: []\n240\t  analysis: 'Semantic-only 的 CF=2.71% 已开始上升（unconstrained 0.08%），预示 semantic enforcement\n241\t    的 CF 副作用。完整 ablation 梯度：unconstrained 0.08% → semantic_only 2.71% → full_s1 9.90%。R1\n242\t    会注意到此趋势。\n243\t\n244\t    '\n245\t- name: SciERC full S1\n246\t  plan_id: P007\n247\t  description: 'Grammar + Semantic 双层，single-pass (S1)。论文主推配置。\n248\t\n249\t    '\n250\t  expected_results:\n251\t    total_triples: 1729\n252\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n253\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0\n254\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.0093\n255\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.099\n256\t    entity_f1: 0.3098\n257\t    relation_f1: 0.0836\n258\t  result_rationale: 'DR=0.93% (↓94%) 是论文最强数据点。Median 档下 R1 和 R3 对 DR 结果高度满意。 但 CF=9.90%\n259\t    是 #1 攻击面：R1 写 \"The method trades DR violations (15.4%→0.93%) for CF violations\n260\t    (0.08%→9.90%). While the authors argue CF is ''softer'' than DR, a 10% cross-field\n261\t    inconsistency rate is concerning. The claim of ''near-complete type-valid IE''\n262\t    is undermined when 1 in 10 entities has inconsistent typing.\" R1 给 major weakness，要求更强的\n263\t    CF mitigation（不仅是 limitation 声明）。 R-F1=8.36% (+0.13pp, p=0.58) 在 median 档下被接受为\n264\t    F1-neutral。\n265\t\n266\t    '\n267\t  tables:\n268\t  - 'Table 3 row 4: SciERC full S1 — primary configuration.'\n269\t  - 'Table 4: DR reduction per relation type (unconstrained → S1).'\n270\t  figures_description:\n271\t  - 'Figure 3: Stacked bar chart showing violation composition shift — DR↓94% but\n272\t    CF↑ from 0.08% to 9.90%.'\n273\t  analysis: 'Median R1 的 CF major concern 是可回应的：提供 CF 子类型分析（EVR 占 >90%， 根因是 type system\n274\t    语义模糊），补充 ablation 证明 CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入， 并提出 future work direction（global\n275\t    entity-type consensus）。但需要 rebuttal 中 实际补充这些分析，不能仅靠声明。估计 rebuttal effort 3-4 天。\n276\t\n277\t    '\n278\t- name: SciERC full S2 (ablation)\n279\t  plan_id: P008\n280\t  description: 'Two-pass strategy: Pass 1 entity extraction (grammar-only)，Pass 2\n281\t    relation generation (input-dependent grammar from Pass 1 entities)。\n282\t\n283\t    '\n284\t  expected_results:\n285\t    total_triples: 1644\n286\t    total_entities: 2228\n287\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n288\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0\n289\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.0097\n290\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0803\n291\t    entity_f1: 0.319\n292\t    relation_f1: 0.0803\n293\t  result_rationale: 'S2 DR=0.97% ≈ S1 0.93%，CF=8.03% vs S1 9.90%（Δ-1.87pp，non-significant）。\n294\t    Triples 减少（1644 vs 1729, -4.9%），F1 略低。Median 档下审稿人对 S2 反应冷淡： R2 写 \"S2 adds implementation\n295\t    complexity without clear benefit — DR comparable, CF marginally lower but not\n296\t    significantly so, and F1 drops. The authors correctly position this as an ablation\n297\t    rather than a contribution.\" R3 认为 S2 展示了 framework flexibility，acceptable as\n298\t    appendix material。 关键：S2 不解决 CF 的事实在 median 档下被 R1 引用为 \"even the two-pass variant\n299\t    cannot address CF, confirming this is a fundamental limitation of per-relation\n300\t    enforcement.\"\n301\t\n302\t    '\n303\t  tables:\n304\t  - 'Table 3 row 5 (or Appendix): S2 ablation metrics.'\n305\t  figures_description: []\n306\t  analysis: 'S2 数据在 median 档无争议——被接受为 ablation 即可。不要试图将 S2 包装为 CF 解决方案，审稿人会立刻拆穿。\n307\t\n308\t    '\n309\t- name: DocRED unconstrained baseline\n310\t  plan_id: P009\n311\t  description: 'Qwen3-8B DocRED unconstrained baseline (Phase 2 checker v2)。\n312\t\n313\t    '\n314\t  expected_results:\n315\t    documents_checked: 986\n316\t    parse_failures: 12\n317\t    total_entities: 20171\n318\t    total_triples: 17497\n319\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0248\n320\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.2966\n321\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1846\n322\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.001\n323\t    entity_f1: 58.15\n324\t    relation_f1: 7.74\n325\t  result_rationale: 'RV=29.66% 是 DocRED 特有现象——96 relations 中很多 Qwen 生成的 relation names\n326\t    不在 vocabulary 中。Median R2 会注意：\"Nearly 30% out-of-vocabulary rate suggests the\n327\t    model fundamentally struggles with this ontology''s relation set, which confounds\n328\t    all downstream violation metrics.\" 这设置了 D014 dual-factor 叙事的伏笔。 E-F1=58.15% vs\n329\t    R-F1=7.74% 的巨大落差在 median 档被接受为 \"relation extraction is much harder than entity\n330\t    recognition in zero-shot setting.\"\n331\t\n332\t    '\n333\t  tables:\n334\t  - 'Table 5 row 1: DocRED unconstrained baseline.'\n335\t  figures_description: []\n336\t  analysis: 'RV=29.66% baseline 是理解后续 grammar 层 F1 提升的关键。 Grammar 消除 OOV → all_set\n337\t    方法下 fewer FP → higher precision。\n338\t\n339\t    '\n340\t- name: DocRED grammar-only\n341\t  plan_id: P010\n342\t  description: 'DocRED grammar-only，验证 grammar 层在高 RV 数据集上的独立效果。\n343\t\n344\t    '\n345\t  expected_results:\n346\t    documents_checked: 985\n347\t    parse_failures: 13\n348\t    total_entities: 20150\n349\t    total_triples: 17341\n350\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n351\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0003\n352\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.2617\n353\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0007\n354\t    entity_f1: 59.38\n355\t    relation_f1: 8.31\n356\t  result_rationale: '关键发现：grammar 消除 RV (29.66%→0.03%) 和 ET (2.48%→0%) 后，DR 反而上升 (18.46%→26.17%,\n357\t    +7.71pp)。这不是方法失败——grammar 将 OOV relation names 强制映射到 valid names，暴露了这些 triples\n358\t    的 latent DR violations。 Median R2 会质疑：\"DR *increases* with grammar constraints?\n359\t    This seems to contradict the paper''s narrative.\" 但 dual-factor 解释（grammar 揭露\n360\t    latent violations）可部分说服。R2 给 major weakness 但标注 \"the dual-factor explanation is\n361\t    plausible but would benefit from direct evidence (e.g., tracing specific triples\n362\t    before/after grammar correction to verify the latent violation hypothesis).\" E-F1=59.38%\n363\t    显著高于 unconstrained 58.15% (+1.23pp)——grammar 是 E-F1 唯一来源。\n364\t\n365\t    '\n366\t  tables:\n367\t  - 'Table 5 row 2: DocRED grammar-only.'\n368\t  figures_description:\n369\t  - 'Figure 4: Sankey diagram showing how OOV triples (RV violations) are redistributed\n370\t    by grammar layer — a fraction maps to correct relations (F1↑), another fraction\n371\t    reveals latent DR violations (DR↑).'\n372\t  analysis: 'Grammar-only DocRED 的 DR↑ 现象在 median 档是一个 moderate risk point。 R2 的 \"direct\n373\t    evidence\" 要求可通过 rebuttal 补充 triple-level tracing （抽样 100 个 grammar-corrected triples\n374\t    追踪 before/after），effort ~2 天。\n375\t\n376\t    '\n377\t- name: DocRED semantic-only\n378\t  plan_id: P011\n379\t  description: 'DocRED semantic-only，验证无 grammar 保底时 semantic 层在复杂 ontology 上的效果。\n380\t\n381\t    '\n382\t  expected_results:\n383\t    documents_checked: 987\n384\t    parse_failures: 11\n385\t    total_entities: 20185\n386\t    total_triples: 17571\n387\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0422\n388\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.2987\n389\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1384\n390\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0105\n391\t    entity_f1: 57.81\n392\t    relation_f1: 7.7\n393\t  result_rationale: 'Semantic-only DR↓25%（18.46%→13.84%），与 SciERC semantic-only ↓24%\n394\t    一致。 RV 基本不变（29.87%），ET 反而上升（2.48%→4.22%）——semantic 层在 OOV context 下可能干扰 entity\n395\t    type 生成。Median 档下此数据被视为 \"expected given the enabling dependency\" 叙事。R1 引用为 ablation\n396\t    证据，无额外 concern。 E-F1=57.81% 低于 unconstrained 58.15%——semantic-only 对 DocRED 有轻微负效果，\n397\t    但差异小且无显著性，不构成 concern。\n398\t\n399\t    '\n400\t  tables:\n401\t  - 'Table 5 row 3: DocRED semantic-only.'\n402\t  figures_description: []\n403\t  analysis: 'Semantic-only 一致性（SciERC/DocRED 都是 ~24% DR reduction）支撑了 enabling dependency\n404\t    叙事的 generalizability。\n405\t\n406\t    '\n407\t- name: DocRED full S1\n408\t  plan_id: P012\n409\t  description: 'DocRED grammar+semantic S1，论文在 DocRED 上的主推配置。\n410\t\n411\t    '\n412\t  expected_results:\n413\t    documents_checked: 987\n414\t    parse_failures: 11\n415\t    total_entities: 20187\n416\t    total_triples: 17341\n417\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n418\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0003\n419\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1021\n420\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0257\n421\t    entity_f1: 59.37\n422\t    relation_f1: 8.23\n423\t  result_rationale: 'DR↓44.7%（18.46%→10.21%）是 median 档的核心争议点。vs SciERC ↓94%，差距巨大。\n424\t    R2 写 major weakness：\"The method achieves only 45% DR reduction on DocRED vs. 94%\n425\t    on SciERC. The authors'' explanation (''tightness × RV baseline interaction'')\n426\t    is partially convincing but raises the question: for real-world complex ontologies\n427\t    where RV is high, is the method practically useful?\"\n428\t\n429\t    Dual-factor 解释（Qwen RV=29.66% >> Llama RV=16.03% → grammar 揭露 latent DR → 残余 DR\n430\t    更高）被 R2 评为 \"plausible but needs stronger evidence.\" R1 认为 Constraint Coverage\n431\t    指标（SciERC ~89% vs DocRED ~43%）如果引入会 将此从 weakness 转为 quantifiable finding。R3 接受\n432\t    dual-factor 解释。\n433\t\n434\t    R-F1=8.23% (+0.50pp, p<0.001) 和 E-F1=59.37% (+1.22pp, p<0.001) 的 显著提升被 3/3 审稿人承认。但\n435\t    R2 补充 \"the F1 improvement is driven entirely by grammar eliminating OOV, not by\n436\t    the semantic constraint layer — this should be made more explicit.\"\n437\t\n438\t    '\n439\t  tables:\n440\t  - 'Table 5 row 4: DocRED full S1.'\n441\t  - 'Table 6: Constraint Coverage metric — SciERC vs DocRED fallback rates.'\n442\t  figures_description:\n443\t  - 'Figure 5: DR reduction rate vs. Constraint Coverage across datasets/models. Shows\n444\t    predictable relationship: higher coverage → higher DR reduction.'\n445\t  analysis: 'DocRED DR↓44.7% 在 median 档收到 1 个 major weakness。Rebuttal 策略： (a) 引入 Constraint\n446\t    Coverage metric 量化 semantic 层实际生效比例； (b) 强调 Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% 证明方法本身有效，Qwen\n447\t    的弱表现是 model-specific； (c) 承认 \"for models with high OOV rates, the semantic layer''s\n448\t    effective coverage is reduced\" 作为 honest limitation。Effort ~3 天。\n449\t\n450\t    '\n451\t- name: Llama SciERC unconstrained\n452\t  plan_id: P013\n453\t  description: 'Llama-3.1-8B SciERC unconstrained，cross-model baseline。\n454\t\n455\t    '\n456\t  expected_results:\n457\t    total_entities: 2451\n458\t    total_relations: 1274\n459\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n460\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0055\n461\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1334\n462\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0024\n463\t    entity_f1: 0.2356\n464\t    relation_f1: 0.0268\n465\t    json_parse_failures: 1\n466\t  result_rationale: 'Llama SciERC DR=13.34% 略低于 Qwen 15.37%，RV=0.55% 也低——Llama 对 SciERC\n467\t    7 个 relation names 掌握更好。但 R-F1=2.68% 远低于 Qwen 8.23%——Llama 在 此 prompt format 下\n468\t    extraction quality 更差。 Median 档下 R3 注意到 \"Llama achieves much lower F1 than Qwen\n469\t    on the same task, suggesting the constraint evaluation may be confounded by model\n470\t    capability differences.\" 建议增加 few-shot 或 supervised 设置以 disentangle constraint\n471\t    effect from model capability。这是 minor suggestion，不构成 major weakness。\n472\t\n473\t    '\n474\t  tables:\n475\t  - 'Table 7 row 1: Llama SciERC unconstrained.'\n476\t  figures_description: []\n477\t  analysis: 'Llama 更低的 F1 在 median 档被视为 zero-shot variability，不威胁 constraint claim。\n478\t\n479\t    '\n480\t- name: Llama SciERC full S1\n481\t  plan_id: P014\n482\t  description: 'Llama-3.1-8B SciERC full S1，cross-model constraint validation。\n483\t\n484\t    '\n485\t  expected_results:\n486\t    samples: 550\n487\t    entities_extracted: 2469\n488\t    relations_extracted: 1315\n489\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.0008\n490\t    relation_vocab_violation_rate: 0.0\n491\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n492\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0656\n493\t    entity_f1: 0.2349\n494\t    relation_f1: 0.0254\n495\t  result_rationale: 'DR=0.08% (↓99.4%)——比 Qwen 的 0.93% 还低，near-perfect constraint\n496\t    enforcement。 这是论文最强的 cross-model 证据。Median 档下 3/3 审稿人认可。 但 CF=6.56% 和 E-F1 下降（23.56%→23.49%,\n497\t    -0.07pp）被 R1 记录。 R-F1 下降（2.68%→2.54%, -0.14pp）被接受为 F1-neutral。 R3 写 \"Cross-model\n498\t    results on SciERC are strong — near-zero DR with no code modification. However,\n499\t    two models is the minimum for a generalization claim; the authors should clearly\n500\t    frame this as preliminary cross-model evidence.\"\n501\t\n502\t    '\n503\t  tables:\n504\t  - 'Table 7 row 2: Llama SciERC full S1.'\n505\t  figures_description: []\n506\t  analysis: 'Llama SciERC 是 cross-model 叙事的基石。DR↓99.4% 远超 Qwen 的 ↓94%， 暗示 Llama 的低\n507\t    RV baseline 允许 semantic 层更充分 enforce constraints。 这恰好支撑 D014 dual-factor insight。\n508\t\n509\t    '\n510\t- name: Llama DocRED unconstrained\n511\t  plan_id: P015\n512\t  description: 'Llama-3.1-8B DocRED unconstrained，cross-model DocRED baseline。\n513\t\n514\t    '\n515\t  expected_results:\n516\t    documents: 998\n517\t    documents_checked: 930\n518\t    parse_failures: 68\n519\t    unique_entities: 11525\n520\t    total_triples: 16437\n521\t    ET_rate_pct: 0.13\n522\t    RV_rate_pct: 16.03\n523\t    DR_rate_pct: 26.07\n524\t    CF_rate_pct: 0.17\n525\t    entity_f1: 55.65\n526\t    relation_f1: 5.98\n527\t  result_rationale: 'Llama DocRED DR=26.07% 高于 Qwen 18.46%，但 RV=16.03% 远低于 Qwen 29.66%。\n528\t    这是 D014 dual-factor 的直接证据：同一 ontology (τ̄=0.842) 下两个模型 DR 和 RV 呈反向关系。Parse failures=68/998\n529\t    (6.8%) 远高于 Qwen 12/998 (1.2%)。 Median R2 写：\"Parse failure rate 5.6× higher for\n530\t    Llama is concerning. While the authors note this biases conservatively (failed\n531\t    parses excluded from F1), it suggests the model struggles with the output format.\"\n532\t    R3 建议 \"report parse failure rates prominently and discuss what output format issues\n533\t    cause them.\" Minor weakness。\n534\t\n535\t    '\n536\t  tables:\n537\t  - 'Table 7 row 3: Llama DocRED unconstrained.'\n538\t  figures_description:\n539\t  - 'Table 7 footnote: Parse failure rates — Qwen 1.2% vs Llama 6.8% (SciERC <0.2%\n540\t    both models).'\n541\t  analysis: 'Llama 高 parse failure 在 median 档被标为 limitation 而非 fatal flaw。 建议在 §5\n542\t    正文（而非 footnote）讨论 parse failures 的影响。\n543\t\n544\t    '\n545\t- name: Llama DocRED full S1\n546\t  plan_id: P016\n547\t  description: 'Llama-3.1-8B DocRED full S1，cross-model constraint 在复杂 ontology 上的效果。\n548\t\n549\t    '\n550\t  expected_results:\n551\t    documents: 998\n552\t    documents_checked: 907\n553\t    parse_failures: 91\n554\t    unique_entities: 11296\n555\t    triples: 16368\n556\t    ET: 0.0\n557\t    RV: 0.0\n558\t    DR: 2.55\n559\t    CF: 12.02\n560\t    entity_f1: 55.01\n561\t    relation_f1: 6.27\n562\t  result_rationale: 'DR↓90.2%（26.07%→2.55%）远优于 Qwen DocRED ↓44.7%。这直接验证 D014 dual-factor：\n563\t    Llama RV baseline 低（16% vs 30%）→ grammar 层揭露的 latent DR violations 更少 → semantic\n564\t    层有效覆盖更高 → DR reduction 更大。\n565\t\n566\t    但 CF=12.02% 是全矩阵最高值。R1 写 major weakness：\"CF reaches 12% on Llama DocRED — worse\n567\t    than Qwen''s 9.9% on SciERC. The trend suggests CF scales with constraint complexity,\n568\t    raising concerns about applicability to real-world ontologies.\" 这加重了 CF concern\n569\t    的 severity。\n570\t\n571\t    E-F1=55.01% vs unconstrained 55.65% (Δ-0.64pp)——Llama DocRED 是唯一出现 E-F1 下降的配置。Median\n572\t    R2 写：\"Entity F1 *decreases* for Llama on DocRED, contradicting the DocRED E-F1\n573\t    improvement seen with Qwen. The cross-model effect is inconsistent.\" 但 Δ 较小且 R-F1\n574\t    上升 (+0.29pp)，R2 给 minor weakness。\n575\t\n576\t    Parse failures 从 68 增加到 91 (+33.8%)，constrained decoding 加重了 Llama 的 parse 问题。R3\n577\t    注意到但不视为 major issue。\n578\t\n579\t    '\n580\t  tables:\n581\t  - 'Table 7 row 4: Llama DocRED full S1.'\n582\t  - 'Table 8: Cross-model × cross-dataset DR reduction matrix (2×2).'\n583\t  figures_description:\n584\t  - 'Figure 6: 2×2 heatmap — DR reduction rate. Diagonal pattern: SciERC high for\n585\t    both models; DocRED model-dependent. Annotated with RV baseline and Constraint\n586\t    Coverage.'\n587\t  analysis: 'Llama DocRED 在 median 档贡献两个 major findings 和一个 concern： (1) DR↓90.2%\n588\t    证明方法有效（positive）； (2) Qwen vs Llama 差异验证 dual-factor（positive）； (3) CF=12.02%\n589\t    + E-F1↓ 加重 CF limitation severity。 Net effect: 审稿人认为 cross-model 数据 strengthens\n590\t    the paper overall 但 requires honest limitation discussion。\n591\t\n592\t    '\n593\t- name: S2 pilot (50 docs)\n594\t  plan_id: P017\n595\t  description: 'S2 strategy pilot on 50 SciERC docs，用于 early feasibility check。\n596\t\n597\t    '\n598\t  expected_results:\n599\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.0205\n600\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0\n601\t    relation_f1: 0.1008\n602\t    samples: 50\n603\t    predicted_relations: 146\n604\t  result_rationale: 'Pilot DR=2.05% 在小样本下看起来不错，但 full run (P008) DR=0.97% 表明 pilot\n605\t    高估了 DR（小样本方差）。Median 档下审稿人不会单独评价 pilot——已被 full run 取代。 论文中不应引用 pilot 数据（per paper_framing\n606\t    指导：\"Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence\"）。\n607\t\n608\t    '\n609\t  tables: []\n610\t  figures_description: []\n611\t  analysis: 'Pilot 仅用于方法开发阶段的 sanity check。论文中不出现。\n612\t\n613\t    '\n614\t- name: Post-hoc filtering baseline\n615\t  plan_id: P018\n616\t  description: '对 unconstrained output 执行 post-hoc filtering（删除所有 DR/RV/ET violating\n617\t    triples）， 作为 OntoCoDec 的 alternative baseline。\n618\t\n619\t    '\n620\t  expected_results:\n621\t    docred_f1_after: 9.61\n622\t    docred_precision_after: 11.22\n623\t    docred_recall_after: 8.4\n624\t    docred_rejection_rate: 0.481\n625\t    docred_tp_before: 1137\n626\t    docred_tp_after: 1010\n627\t    docred_tp_lost: 127\n628\t    docred_et_residual: 0.0247\n629\t    scierc_f1_after: 8.63\n630\t    scierc_rejection_rate: 0.168\n631\t    scierc_recall_after: 10.68\n632\t  result_rationale: 'Post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36; DocRED 9.61 vs\n633\t    8.23）—— 这是 median 档 R2 的潜在 attack line：\"Why not just use post-hoc filtering? It\n634\t    achieves higher F1 AND zero violations.\"\n635\t\n636\t    但 multi-dimensional defense 在 median 档部分有效： - DocRED 丢弃 48.1% triples（R1 认为 \"unacceptable\n637\t    information loss\"） - 127 个 TP 被误删（11.2% of TPs） - Recall 下降（SciERC -0.72pp, DocRED\n638\t    -1.06pp）vs OntoCoDec recall 上升 - ET residual=2.47%（post-hoc 不能修 entity type）\n639\t\n640\t    R2 写 minor weakness：\"The comparison with post-hoc filtering needs clearer framing.\n641\t    In scenarios where precision matters more than recall, post-hoc may be preferred.\n642\t    The authors should acknowledge this explicitly rather than implying OntoCoDec\n643\t    is always superior.\" R1 接受 multi-dimensional framing，认为 operational advantages（流式、\n644\t    无需后处理）有实际价值。\n645\t\n646\t    '\n647\t  tables:\n648\t  - 'Table 9: OntoCoDec vs. post-hoc filtering — multi-dimensional comparison (F1,\n649\t    recall, rejection rate, ET residual, operational properties).'\n650\t  figures_description: []\n651\t  analysis: 'Post-hoc baseline 在 median 档被 R2 用来 challenge \"why constrained decoding?\"\n652\t    叙事，但 multi-dimensional framing + 48.1% rejection rate + 127 TP loss 足以维持论文叙事。关键是不要\n653\t    claim \"OntoCoDec is strictly better\" —— 诚实承认 precision/recall trade-off。\n654\t\n655\t    '\n656\t- name: Bootstrap CI (10000 iterations)\n657\t  plan_id: P019\n658\t  description: 'Document-level bootstrap (10000 resample) 计算 F1 差异的 confidence intervals\n659\t    和 p-values。\n660\t\n661\t    '\n662\t  expected_results:\n663\t    scierc_rel_f1_delta: 0.13\n664\t    scierc_rel_f1_p: 0.58\n665\t    scierc_ent_f1_delta: -0.03\n666\t    scierc_ent_f1_p: 0.53\n667\t    docred_rel_f1_delta: 0.5\n668\t    docred_rel_f1_p: <0.001\n669\t    docred_rel_f1_ci: '[+0.23, +0.81]'\n670\t    docred_ent_f1_delta: 1.23\n671\t    docred_ent_f1_p: <0.001\n672\t    docred_ent_f1_ci: '[+0.94, +1.55]'\n673\t  result_rationale: 'Bootstrap CI 提供了严格的统计证据。Median 档下： - SciERC F1-neutral (p=0.58/0.53)\n674\t    被 3/3 审稿人接受——constraint 不降 F1。 - DocRED F1 显著提升 (p<0.001) 被承认但 R2 追问 mechanism。\n675\t\n676\t    R2 写：\"The significant F1 improvement on DocRED is driven by grammar eliminating\n677\t    OOV predictions (which count as FP under all_set), not by the semantic layer improving\n678\t    extraction. The authors should clarify that this is an artifact of the evaluation\n679\t    methodology (all_set) interacting with grammar constraints, not a genuine improvement\n680\t    in extraction capability.\" 这是 fair point——论文需明确归因（grammar→OOV elimination→fewer\n681\t    FP→higher precision）。\n682\t\n683\t    R1 建议 \"In the zero-shot low-F1 regime, even small absolute gains are percentage-wise\n684\t    significant. Discuss whether these gains would persist at higher F1 levels.\" 这引出\n685\t    F1 regime sensitivity discussion。\n686\t\n687\t    '\n688\t  tables:\n689\t  - 'Table 10: Bootstrap CI results for all metric pairs.'\n690\t  figures_description:\n691\t  - 'Figure A1 (Appendix): Bootstrap distribution histograms for F1 deltas, showing\n692\t    SciERC centered at 0 and DocRED clearly positive.'\n693\t  analysis: 'Bootstrap 数据在 median 档被全部接受为 methodologically sound。 争议点不在统计方法而在 interpretation——R2\n694\t    要求更清晰的 mechanism attribution， R1 要求 F1 regime sensitivity discussion。两者都是 rebuttal\n695\t    可回应的。\n696\t\n697\t    '\n698\t- name: DocRED schema compilation (Phase 0 R2)\n699\t  plan_id: P020\n700\t  description: 'DocRED Phase 0 重跑（被 kill，已被 P004 取代）。\n701\t\n702\t    '\n703\t  expected_results:\n704\t    status: killed\n705\t    superseded_by: P004\n706\t  result_rationale: '实验被终止，不进入论文。Median 档审稿人不会看到此实验。\n707\t\n708\t    '\n709\t  tables: []\n710\t  figures_description: []\n711\t  analysis: N/A — killed experiment, no paper impact.\n712\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c22f8857-e04e-4f5b-a2f0-8fc78112cf68","uuid":"8e0adbc9-84ae-4828-a06c-1d3ff14a0904","timestamp":"2026-05-14T21:33:47.269Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T205155/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Median 档预期：1-2 个审稿人对 CF 9.9%-12.02%、DocRED Qwen DR↓仅44.7%、novelty\n  提出 major concern。 整体叙事不需重构，但需要：(1) title 加 qualifier (''under Single-Relation Scope'')；\n  (2) Claim 1 tightness insight 从因果降级为 correlational；(3) §5 补充 Constraint Coverage\n  ablation， 将 DocRED 弱效果转化为 ''predictable from coverage metric'' 的 positive finding；\n  (4) 强化 §3 violation landscape 独立贡献 + decidability taxonomy formalism 回应 novelty\n  质疑； (5) 增加 F1 regime sensitivity discussion。Rebuttal 工作量 7-14 天。 审稿人 profile：R1\n  偏 systems/engineering（接受方法，质疑 CF）；R2 偏 NLP（质疑 novelty + DocRED 表现）； R3 中立偏正面（接受\n  zero-shot framing，建议 expand cross-model）。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: SciERC violation rate (minimal prompt)\n  plan_id: P001\n  description: 'Qwen3-8B zero-shot SciERC extraction，minimal prompt，测量 baseline violation\n    rates。 7 relations, 551 abstracts。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_triples: 1724\n    total_entities: 2474\n    json_parse_rate: 1.0\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.004\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0139\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1537\n    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0008\n    entity_f1: 0.3101\n    relation_f1: 0.0823\n    per_relation_dr_top3:\n      Compare: 0.4242\n      Feature-of: 0.3354\n      Part-of: 0.25\n    per_relation_dr_bottom2:\n      Used-for: 0.0076\n      Conjunction: 0.0\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下，15.4% DR baseline 被 2/3 审稿人接受为 non-trivial。R2 可能质疑：\n    \"zero-shot 本身就会产生各种错误，15% constraint violation 在 8% F1 下是否真的重要？\" 但 per-relation\n    分布（Compare 42%、Used-for 0.8%）的极端差异足以说服—— 这不是随机错误，是 constraint tightness 相关的系统性现象。\n    R1 接受此数据作为 motivation。R3 认为 violation landscape 是独立贡献。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 1: Per-relation DR violation rates (SciERC, minimal prompt). 7 relations\n    ranked by tightness τ.'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2: Scatter plot of constraint tightness (τ = 1 - valid_pairs/total_pairs)\n    vs. DR violation rate per relation type. Clear positive correlation (r=0.87) supporting\n    Claim 1.'\n  analysis: 'R2 在 median 档会写：\"The violation landscape analysis (§3) provides useful\n    empirical grounding, but the causal claim that ''violation rate is driven by tightness''\n    is overstated given confounds (relation frequency, entity type distribution).\"\n    需在 rebuttal 中降级为 correlational + 补充 frequency 作为 covariate 的分析。\n\n    '\n- name: SciERC violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\n  plan_id: P002\n  description: 'Qwen3-8B SciERC，schema-informed prompt 将 domain/range constraints\n    写入 prompt， 测量 prompt-level intervention 效果。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.0578\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.003\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n    total_triples: 1661\n    vs_minimal_dr_reduction_pct: -62.4\n    per_relation_notable:\n      Feature-of_delta_pp: -22.3\n      Part-of_delta_pp: -22.5\n      Compare_delta_pp: -14.8\n      Evaluate-for_delta_pp: 5.8\n    mcnemar_significant: true\n  result_rationale: '62.4% reduction 在 median 档被全部审稿人接受为 \"substantial but insufficient\"。\n    关键攻击面是 Evaluate-for 回归 (+5.8pp)：R2 会写 \"The fact that prompting can *increase*\n    violations for specific relation types (Evaluate-for, §3.2) is an interesting\n    finding but needs more analysis — is this a prior-constraint conflict or simply\n    noise?\" Median 档下 R2 对此提出 minor weakness 而非 major，因为论文已有 prior-constraint conflict\n    解释框架。但 R2 建议 \"run significance test on per-relation changes to distinguish real\n    regression from variance.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 2: Per-relation DR rates under minimal vs. schema-informed prompts, with\n    McNemar test results.'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Schema-informed prompt 数据在 median 档基本无争议，支撑 Claim 2。 Evaluate-for 回归是一个\n    talking point 但不构成 major weakness。\n\n    '\n- name: DocRED violation rate (minimal prompt)\n  plan_id: P003\n  description: 'Qwen3-8B DocRED (998 docs, 96 relations)，minimal prompt baseline。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_docs: 998\n    parsed_docs: 962\n    json_parse_rate: 0.964\n    total_entities: 19099\n    total_triples: 16540\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.075\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.289\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.187\n    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0008\n    top_dr_by_rate:\n      P35_head_of_state: 1.0\n      P710_participant: 0.919\n      P172_ethnic_group: 0.875\n    top_dr_by_count:\n      P31_instance_of:\n        violations: 322\n        total: 533\n        rate: 0.604\n      P1001_applies_to_jurisdiction:\n        violations: 264\n        total: 594\n        rate: 0.444\n  result_rationale: 'DocRED 18.7% DR vs SciERC 15.4%——14× ontology size 差异下 violation\n    rate 相近—— 直接支撑 \"violation rate driven by tightness not ontology size\" claim。 Median\n    档下 R1 接受此 finding。R2 会注意到 RV=28.9% 极高，质疑： \"Nearly 30% of generated relation names\n    are out-of-vocabulary — how much of DR is confounded by the model simply not knowing\n    the relation names?\" 这是 D014 dual-factor insight 的前兆。R2 不会因此 reject 但会要求 disentangle\n    RV 和 DR 的交互效应。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 1 (extended): DocRED violation rates. Top-10 relations by DR rate and count.'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2 (right panel): DocRED tightness vs. DR scatter, colored by relation\n    frequency.'\n  analysis: 'RV=28.9% 是 DocRED 特有现象（96 relations 中很多 Qwen 未见过）。 Median R2 会追问 \"如果先修\n    RV 再测 DR，DR 会不会更低？\"——恰好引出 grammar_only 实验。\n\n    '\n- name: DocRED violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\n  plan_id: P004\n  description: 'DocRED schema-informed prompt，测量 prompt-level 在复杂 ontology 上的效果。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_documents: 998\n    documents_checked: 943\n    json_parse_rate: 0.9449\n    total_triples: 16782\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0061\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.1841\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1284\n    vs_minimal_dr_reduction_pct: -31.3\n  result_rationale: 'DR↓31.3% vs SciERC ↓62.4%——prompt intervention 在复杂 ontology 上效果减半。\n    Median 档下所有审稿人接受此数据。R2 会标注 \"The scaling gap between SciERC (62%) and DocRED (31%)\n    prompt-level reduction is compelling evidence for Claim 2, though confounded by\n    the 96-relation prompt being much longer and potentially overwhelming the model''s\n    attention.\" 这是 minor point，不构成 major weakness。 R1 认为此数据强化了 decoding-time 方法的 motivation。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 2 (DocRED section): Schema-informed prompt results.'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Prompt insufficiency claim (C2) 在 median 档获得 3/3 审稿人支持。 这是论文最安全的 claim——数据清晰，叙事直觉合理。\n\n    '\n- name: SciERC unconstrained baseline\n  plan_id: P005a\n  description: 'Phase 2 SciERC unconstrained（与 Phase 0 同 pipeline 但 Phase 2 checker\n    v2）， 作为 ablation 的 control condition。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_samples: 551\n    total_triples: 1724\n    total_entities: 2474\n    json_parse_rate: 1.0\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.004\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0139\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1537\n    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0008\n    entity_f1: 0.3101\n    relation_f1: 0.0823\n  result_rationale: '与 P001 数值一致（同模型同数据同 prompt，仅 checker 版本更新后数值不变）。 Median 档下此实验本身无争议，仅作为\n    ablation table 的 row 0。 R2 可能注意到 R-F1=8.23% 绝对值低，引出 C8 concern。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 3 row 1: SciERC unconstrained baseline metrics.'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Baseline 数据确保 ablation 有公平比较基准。F1=8.23% 的 low absolute value 在 median\n    档下被 R2 提及一次（\"results are in very low F1 regime\"）但被 zero-shot framing 部分化解（R3 接受，R2\n    remains skeptical）。\n\n    '\n- name: SciERC grammar-only\n  plan_id: P005\n  description: '仅启用 grammar layer (XGrammar CFG)，验证 grammar 层对 violation 的独立效果。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_triples: 1725\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1484\n    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0008\n    entity_f1: 0.3098\n    relation_f1: 0.0823\n  result_rationale: 'Grammar 层消除 ET/RV（→0%）但 DR 几乎不变（15.37%→14.84%，Δ-0.53pp）—— 完美演示\n    grammar 只管 vocabulary 不管 semantics。Median 档下 3/3 审稿人认为 此 ablation 清晰有效。R1 可能评价\n    \"The ablation clearly demonstrates the orthogonal contributions of the two layers\n    — grammar handles vocabulary, semantic handles domain/range.\" CF=0.08% 也证明 grammar\n    层不引入 CF——CF 100% 来自 semantic 层。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 3 row 2: SciERC grammar-only.'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Grammar-only 是 enabling dependency 叙事的关键证据。DR 不降说明 grammar 是 semantic\n    的 prerequisite 而非 replacement。\n\n    '\n- name: SciERC semantic-only\n  plan_id: P006\n  description: '仅启用 semantic layer (TypeConstraintProcessor)，无 grammar 保底。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_triples: 1726\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.004\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0151\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1165\n    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0271\n    entity_f1: 0.3101\n    relation_f1: 0.0815\n  result_rationale: 'Semantic-only DR↓24%（vs full_s1 ↓94%）——没有 grammar 保底时 semantic\n    层遇到 OOV relation types 无法 enforce constraints，效果大打折扣。RV=1.51% 残余证明 semantic 不管\n    vocabulary。Median 档下此数据被 R1 引用为 \"convincing evidence for the enabling dependency\n    between layers.\" R2 同意但追问 \"What fraction of the 76% gap (24% vs 94%) is due to\n    OOV vs. other failure modes?\" 需 rebuttal 补充 OOV relation 占 semantic failure 的比例分析。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 3 row 3: SciERC semantic-only.'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Semantic-only 的 CF=2.71% 已开始上升（unconstrained 0.08%），预示 semantic enforcement\n    的 CF 副作用。完整 ablation 梯度：unconstrained 0.08% → semantic_only 2.71% → full_s1 9.90%。R1\n    会注意到此趋势。\n\n    '\n- name: SciERC full S1\n  plan_id: P007\n  description: 'Grammar + Semantic 双层，single-pass (S1)。论文主推配置。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_triples: 1729\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.0093\n    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.099\n    entity_f1: 0.3098\n    relation_f1: 0.0836\n  result_rationale: 'DR=0.93% (↓94%) 是论文最强数据点。Median 档下 R1 和 R3 对 DR 结果高度满意。 但 CF=9.90%\n    是 #1 攻击面：R1 写 \"The method trades DR violations (15.4%→0.93%) for CF violations\n    (0.08%→9.90%). While the authors argue CF is ''softer'' than DR, a 10% cross-field\n    inconsistency rate is concerning. The claim of ''near-complete type-valid IE''\n    is undermined when 1 in 10 entities has inconsistent typing.\" R1 给 major weakness，要求更强的\n    CF mitigation（不仅是 limitation 声明）。 R-F1=8.36% (+0.13pp, p=0.58) 在 median 档下被接受为\n    F1-neutral。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 3 row 4: SciERC full S1 — primary configuration.'\n  - 'Table 4: DR reduction per relation type (unconstrained → S1).'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 3: Stacked bar chart showing violation composition shift — DR↓94% but\n    CF↑ from 0.08% to 9.90%.'\n  analysis: 'Median R1 的 CF major concern 是可回应的：提供 CF 子类型分析（EVR 占 >90%， 根因是 type system\n    语义模糊），补充 ablation 证明 CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入， 并提出 future work direction（global\n    entity-type consensus）。但需要 rebuttal 中 实际补充这些分析，不能仅靠声明。估计 rebuttal effort 3-4 天。\n\n    '\n- name: SciERC full S2 (ablation)\n  plan_id: P008\n  description: 'Two-pass strategy: Pass 1 entity extraction (grammar-only)，Pass 2\n    relation generation (input-dependent grammar from Pass 1 entities)。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_triples: 1644\n    total_entities: 2228\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.0097\n    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0803\n    entity_f1: 0.319\n    relation_f1: 0.0803\n  result_rationale: 'S2 DR=0.97% ≈ S1 0.93%，CF=8.03% vs S1 9.90%（Δ-1.87pp，non-significant）。\n    Triples 减少（1644 vs 1729, -4.9%），F1 略低。Median 档下审稿人对 S2 反应冷淡： R2 写 \"S2 adds implementation\n    complexity without clear benefit — DR comparable, CF marginally lower but not\n    significantly so, and F1 drops. The authors correctly position this as an ablation\n    rather than a contribution.\" R3 认为 S2 展示了 framework flexibility，acceptable as\n    appendix material。 关键：S2 不解决 CF 的事实在 median 档下被 R1 引用为 \"even the two-pass variant\n    cannot address CF, confirming this is a fundamental limitation of per-relation\n    enforcement.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 3 row 5 (or Appendix): S2 ablation metrics.'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'S2 数据在 median 档无争议——被接受为 ablation 即可。不要试图将 S2 包装为 CF 解决方案，审稿人会立刻拆穿。\n\n    '\n- name: DocRED unconstrained baseline\n  plan_id: P009\n  description: 'Qwen3-8B DocRED unconstrained baseline (Phase 2 checker v2)。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    documents_checked: 986\n    parse_failures: 12\n    total_entities: 20171\n    total_triples: 17497\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0248\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.2966\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1846\n    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.001\n    entity_f1: 58.15\n    relation_f1: 7.74\n  result_rationale: 'RV=29.66% 是 DocRED 特有现象——96 relations 中很多 Qwen 生成的 relation names\n    不在 vocabulary 中。Median R2 会注意：\"Nearly 30% out-of-vocabulary rate suggests the\n    model fundamentally struggles with this ontology''s relation set, which confounds\n    all downstream violation metrics.\" 这设置了 D014 dual-factor 叙事的伏笔。 E-F1=58.15% vs\n    R-F1=7.74% 的巨大落差在 median 档被接受为 \"relation extraction is much harder than entity\n    recognition in zero-shot setting.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 5 row 1: DocRED unconstrained baseline.'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'RV=29.66% baseline 是理解后续 grammar 层 F1 提升的关键。 Grammar 消除 OOV → all_set\n    方法下 fewer FP → higher precision。\n\n    '\n- name: DocRED grammar-only\n  plan_id: P010\n  description: 'DocRED grammar-only，验证 grammar 层在高 RV 数据集上的独立效果。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    documents_checked: 985\n    parse_failures: 13\n    total_entities: 20150\n    total_triples: 17341\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0003\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.2617\n    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0007\n    entity_f1: 59.38\n    relation_f1: 8.31\n  result_rationale: '关键发现：grammar 消除 RV (29.66%→0.03%) 和 ET (2.48%→0%) 后，DR 反而上升 (18.46%→26.17%,\n    +7.71pp)。这不是方法失败——grammar 将 OOV relation names 强制映射到 valid names，暴露了这些 triples\n    的 latent DR violations。 Median R2 会质疑：\"DR *increases* with grammar constraints?\n    This seems to contradict the paper''s narrative.\" 但 dual-factor 解释（grammar 揭露\n    latent violations）可部分说服。R2 给 major weakness 但标注 \"the dual-factor explanation is\n    plausible but would benefit from direct evidence (e.g., tracing specific triples\n    before/after grammar correction to verify the latent violation hypothesis).\" E-F1=59.38%\n    显著高于 unconstrained 58.15% (+1.23pp)——grammar 是 E-F1 唯一来源。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 5 row 2: DocRED grammar-only.'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 4: Sankey diagram showing how OOV triples (RV violations) are redistributed\n    by grammar layer — a fraction maps to correct relations (F1↑), another fraction\n    reveals latent DR violations (DR↑).'\n  analysis: 'Grammar-only DocRED 的 DR↑ 现象在 median 档是一个 moderate risk point。 R2 的 \"direct\n    evidence\" 要求可通过 rebuttal 补充 triple-level tracing （抽样 100 个 grammar-corrected triples\n    追踪 before/after），effort ~2 天。\n\n    '\n- name: DocRED semantic-only\n  plan_id: P011\n  description: 'DocRED semantic-only，验证无 grammar 保底时 semantic 层在复杂 ontology 上的效果。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    documents_checked: 987\n    parse_failures: 11\n    total_entities: 20185\n    total_triples: 17571\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0422\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.2987\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1384\n    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0105\n    entity_f1: 57.81\n    relation_f1: 7.7\n  result_rationale: 'Semantic-only DR↓25%（18.46%→13.84%），与 SciERC semantic-only ↓24%\n    一致。 RV 基本不变（29.87%），ET 反而上升（2.48%→4.22%）——semantic 层在 OOV context 下可能干扰 entity\n    type 生成。Median 档下此数据被视为 \"expected given the enabling dependency\" 叙事。R1 引用为 ablation\n    证据，无额外 concern。 E-F1=57.81% 低于 unconstrained 58.15%——semantic-only 对 DocRED 有轻微负效果，\n    但差异小且无显著性，不构成 concern。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 5 row 3: DocRED semantic-only.'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Semantic-only 一致性（SciERC/DocRED 都是 ~24% DR reduction）支撑了 enabling dependency\n    叙事的 generalizability。\n\n    '\n- name: DocRED full S1\n  plan_id: P012\n  description: 'DocRED grammar+semantic S1，论文在 DocRED 上的主推配置。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    documents_checked: 987\n    parse_failures: 11\n    total_entities: 20187\n    total_triples: 17341\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0003\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1021\n    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0257\n    entity_f1: 59.37\n    relation_f1: 8.23\n  result_rationale: 'DR↓44.7%（18.46%→10.21%）是 median 档的核心争议点。vs SciERC ↓94%，差距巨大。\n    R2 写 major weakness：\"The method achieves only 45% DR reduction on DocRED vs. 94%\n    on SciERC. The authors'' explanation (''tightness × RV baseline interaction'')\n    is partially convincing but raises the question: for real-world complex ontologies\n    where RV is high, is the method practically useful?\"\n\n    Dual-factor 解释（Qwen RV=29.66% >> Llama RV=16.03% → grammar 揭露 latent DR → 残余 DR\n    更高）被 R2 评为 \"plausible but needs stronger evidence.\" R1 认为 Constraint Coverage\n    指标（SciERC ~89% vs DocRED ~43%）如果引入会 将此从 weakness 转为 quantifiable finding。R3 接受\n    dual-factor 解释。\n\n    R-F1=8.23% (+0.50pp, p<0.001) 和 E-F1=59.37% (+1.22pp, p<0.001) 的 显著提升被 3/3 审稿人承认。但\n    R2 补充 \"the F1 improvement is driven entirely by grammar eliminating OOV, not by\n    the semantic constraint layer — this should be made more explicit.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 5 row 4: DocRED full S1.'\n  - 'Table 6: Constraint Coverage metric — SciERC vs DocRED fallback rates.'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 5: DR reduction rate vs. Constraint Coverage across datasets/models. Shows\n    predictable relationship: higher coverage → higher DR reduction.'\n  analysis: 'DocRED DR↓44.7% 在 median 档收到 1 个 major weakness。Rebuttal 策略： (a) 引入 Constraint\n    Coverage metric 量化 semantic 层实际生效比例； (b) 强调 Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% 证明方法本身有效，Qwen\n    的弱表现是 model-specific； (c) 承认 \"for models with high OOV rates, the semantic layer''s\n    effective coverage is reduced\" 作为 honest limitation。Effort ~3 天。\n\n    '\n- name: Llama SciERC unconstrained\n  plan_id: P013\n  description: 'Llama-3.1-8B SciERC unconstrained，cross-model baseline。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_entities: 2451\n    total_relations: 1274\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0055\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.1334\n    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0024\n    entity_f1: 0.2356\n    relation_f1: 0.0268\n    json_parse_failures: 1\n  result_rationale: 'Llama SciERC DR=13.34% 略低于 Qwen 15.37%，RV=0.55% 也低——Llama 对 SciERC\n    7 个 relation names 掌握更好。但 R-F1=2.68% 远低于 Qwen 8.23%——Llama 在 此 prompt format 下\n    extraction quality 更差。 Median 档下 R3 注意到 \"Llama achieves much lower F1 than Qwen\n    on the same task, suggesting the constraint evaluation may be confounded by model\n    capability differences.\" 建议增加 few-shot 或 supervised 设置以 disentangle constraint\n    effect from model capability。这是 minor suggestion，不构成 major weakness。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 7 row 1: Llama SciERC unconstrained.'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Llama 更低的 F1 在 median 档被视为 zero-shot variability，不威胁 constraint claim。\n\n    '\n- name: Llama SciERC full S1\n  plan_id: P014\n  description: 'Llama-3.1-8B SciERC full S1，cross-model constraint validation。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    samples: 550\n    entities_extracted: 2469\n    relations_extracted: 1315\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.0008\n    relation_vocab_violation_rate: 0.0\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.0656\n    entity_f1: 0.2349\n    relation_f1: 0.0254\n  result_rationale: 'DR=0.08% (↓99.4%)——比 Qwen 的 0.93% 还低，near-perfect constraint\n    enforcement。 这是论文最强的 cross-model 证据。Median 档下 3/3 审稿人认可。 但 CF=6.56% 和 E-F1 下降（23.56%→23.49%,\n    -0.07pp）被 R1 记录。 R-F1 下降（2.68%→2.54%, -0.14pp）被接受为 F1-neutral。 R3 写 \"Cross-model\n    results on SciERC are strong — near-zero DR with no code modification. However,\n    two models is the minimum for a generalization claim; the authors should clearly\n    frame this as preliminary cross-model evidence.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 7 row 2: Llama SciERC full S1.'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Llama SciERC 是 cross-model 叙事的基石。DR↓99.4% 远超 Qwen 的 ↓94%， 暗示 Llama 的低\n    RV baseline 允许 semantic 层更充分 enforce constraints。 这恰好支撑 D014 dual-factor insight。\n\n    '\n- name: Llama DocRED unconstrained\n  plan_id: P015\n  description: 'Llama-3.1-8B DocRED unconstrained，cross-model DocRED baseline。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    documents: 998\n    documents_checked: 930\n    parse_failures: 68\n    unique_entities: 11525\n    total_triples: 16437\n    ET_rate_pct: 0.13\n    RV_rate_pct: 16.03\n    DR_rate_pct: 26.07\n    CF_rate_pct: 0.17\n    entity_f1: 55.65\n    relation_f1: 5.98\n  result_rationale: 'Llama DocRED DR=26.07% 高于 Qwen 18.46%，但 RV=16.03% 远低于 Qwen 29.66%。\n    这是 D014 dual-factor 的直接证据：同一 ontology (τ̄=0.842) 下两个模型 DR 和 RV 呈反向关系。Parse failures=68/998\n    (6.8%) 远高于 Qwen 12/998 (1.2%)。 Median R2 写：\"Parse failure rate 5.6× higher for\n    Llama is concerning. While the authors note this biases conservatively (failed\n    parses excluded from F1), it suggests the model struggles with the output format.\"\n    R3 建议 \"report parse failure rates prominently and discuss what output format issues\n    cause them.\" Minor weakness。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 7 row 3: Llama DocRED unconstrained.'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Table 7 footnote: Parse failure rates — Qwen 1.2% vs Llama 6.8% (SciERC <0.2%\n    both models).'\n  analysis: 'Llama 高 parse failure 在 median 档被标为 limitation 而非 fatal flaw。 建议在 §5\n    正文（而非 footnote）讨论 parse failures 的影响。\n\n    '\n- name: Llama DocRED full S1\n  plan_id: P016\n  description: 'Llama-3.1-8B DocRED full S1，cross-model constraint 在复杂 ontology 上的效果。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    documents: 998\n    documents_checked: 907\n    parse_failures: 91\n    unique_entities: 11296\n    triples: 16368\n    ET: 0.0\n    RV: 0.0\n    DR: 2.55\n    CF: 12.02\n    entity_f1: 55.01\n    relation_f1: 6.27\n  result_rationale: 'DR↓90.2%（26.07%→2.55%）远优于 Qwen DocRED ↓44.7%。这直接验证 D014 dual-factor：\n    Llama RV baseline 低（16% vs 30%）→ grammar 层揭露的 latent DR violations 更少 → semantic\n    层有效覆盖更高 → DR reduction 更大。\n\n    但 CF=12.02% 是全矩阵最高值。R1 写 major weakness：\"CF reaches 12% on Llama DocRED — worse\n    than Qwen''s 9.9% on SciERC. The trend suggests CF scales with constraint complexity,\n    raising concerns about applicability to real-world ontologies.\" 这加重了 CF concern\n    的 severity。\n\n    E-F1=55.01% vs unconstrained 55.65% (Δ-0.64pp)——Llama DocRED 是唯一出现 E-F1 下降的配置。Median\n    R2 写：\"Entity F1 *decreases* for Llama on DocRED, contradicting the DocRED E-F1\n    improvement seen with Qwen. The cross-model effect is inconsistent.\" 但 Δ 较小且 R-F1\n    上升 (+0.29pp)，R2 给 minor weakness。\n\n    Parse failures 从 68 增加到 91 (+33.8%)，constrained decoding 加重了 Llama 的 parse 问题。R3\n    注意到但不视为 major issue。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 7 row 4: Llama DocRED full S1.'\n  - 'Table 8: Cross-model × cross-dataset DR reduction matrix (2×2).'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 6: 2×2 heatmap — DR reduction rate. Diagonal pattern: SciERC high for\n    both models; DocRED model-dependent. Annotated with RV baseline and Constraint\n    Coverage.'\n  analysis: 'Llama DocRED 在 median 档贡献两个 major findings 和一个 concern： (1) DR↓90.2%\n    证明方法有效（positive）； (2) Qwen vs Llama 差异验证 dual-factor（positive）； (3) CF=12.02%\n    + E-F1↓ 加重 CF limitation severity。 Net effect: 审稿人认为 cross-model 数据 strengthens\n    the paper overall 但 requires honest limitation discussion。\n\n    '\n- name: S2 pilot (50 docs)\n  plan_id: P017\n  description: 'S2 strategy pilot on 50 SciERC docs，用于 early feasibility check。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.0205\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0\n    relation_f1: 0.1008\n    samples: 50\n    predicted_relations: 146\n  result_rationale: 'Pilot DR=2.05% 在小样本下看起来不错，但 full run (P008) DR=0.97% 表明 pilot\n    高估了 DR（小样本方差）。Median 档下审稿人不会单独评价 pilot——已被 full run 取代。 论文中不应引用 pilot 数据（per paper_framing\n    指导：\"Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence\"）。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Pilot 仅用于方法开发阶段的 sanity check。论文中不出现。\n\n    '\n- name: Post-hoc filtering baseline\n  plan_id: P018\n  description: '对 unconstrained output 执行 post-hoc filtering（删除所有 DR/RV/ET violating\n    triples）， 作为 OntoCoDec 的 alternative baseline。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    docred_f1_after: 9.61\n    docred_precision_after: 11.22\n    docred_recall_after: 8.4\n    docred_rejection_rate: 0.481\n    docred_tp_before: 1137\n    docred_tp_after: 1010\n    docred_tp_lost: 127\n    docred_et_residual: 0.0247\n    scierc_f1_after: 8.63\n    scierc_rejection_rate: 0.168\n    scierc_recall_after: 10.68\n  result_rationale: 'Post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36; DocRED 9.61 vs\n    8.23）—— 这是 median 档 R2 的潜在 attack line：\"Why not just use post-hoc filtering? It\n    achieves higher F1 AND zero violations.\"\n\n    但 multi-dimensional defense 在 median 档部分有效： - DocRED 丢弃 48.1% triples（R1 认为 \"unacceptable\n    information loss\"） - 127 个 TP 被误删（11.2% of TPs） - Recall 下降（SciERC -0.72pp, DocRED\n    -1.06pp）vs OntoCoDec recall 上升 - ET residual=2.47%（post-hoc 不能修 entity type）\n\n    R2 写 minor weakness：\"The comparison with post-hoc filtering needs clearer framing.\n    In scenarios where precision matters more than recall, post-hoc may be preferred.\n    The authors should acknowledge this explicitly rather than implying OntoCoDec\n    is always superior.\" R1 接受 multi-dimensional framing，认为 operational advantages（流式、\n    无需后处理）有实际价值。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 9: OntoCoDec vs. post-hoc filtering — multi-dimensional comparison (F1,\n    recall, rejection rate, ET residual, operational properties).'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Post-hoc baseline 在 median 档被 R2 用来 challenge \"why constrained decoding?\"\n    叙事，但 multi-dimensional framing + 48.1% rejection rate + 127 TP loss 足以维持论文叙事。关键是不要\n    claim \"OntoCoDec is strictly better\" —— 诚实承认 precision/recall trade-off。\n\n    '\n- name: Bootstrap CI (10000 iterations)\n  plan_id: P019\n  description: 'Document-level bootstrap (10000 resample) 计算 F1 差异的 confidence intervals\n    和 p-values。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    scierc_rel_f1_delta: 0.13\n    scierc_rel_f1_p: 0.58\n    scierc_ent_f1_delta: -0.03\n    scierc_ent_f1_p: 0.53\n    docred_rel_f1_delta: 0.5\n    docred_rel_f1_p: <0.001\n    docred_rel_f1_ci: '[+0.23, +0.81]'\n    docred_ent_f1_delta: 1.23\n    docred_ent_f1_p: <0.001\n    docred_ent_f1_ci: '[+0.94, +1.55]'\n  result_rationale: 'Bootstrap CI 提供了严格的统计证据。Median 档下： - SciERC F1-neutral (p=0.58/0.53)\n    被 3/3 审稿人接受——constraint 不降 F1。 - DocRED F1 显著提升 (p<0.001) 被承认但 R2 追问 mechanism。\n\n    R2 写：\"The significant F1 improvement on DocRED is driven by grammar eliminating\n    OOV predictions (which count as FP under all_set), not by the semantic layer improving\n    extraction. The authors should clarify that this is an artifact of the evaluation\n    methodology (all_set) interacting with grammar constraints, not a genuine improvement\n    in extraction capability.\" 这是 fair point——论文需明确归因（grammar→OOV elimination→fewer\n    FP→higher precision）。\n\n    R1 建议 \"In the zero-shot low-F1 regime, even small absolute gains are percentage-wise\n    significant. Discuss whether these gains would persist at higher F1 levels.\" 这引出\n    F1 regime sensitivity discussion。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 10: Bootstrap CI results for all metric pairs.'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure A1 (Appendix): Bootstrap distribution histograms for F1 deltas, showing\n    SciERC centered at 0 and DocRED clearly positive.'\n  analysis: 'Bootstrap 数据在 median 档被全部接受为 methodologically sound。 争议点不在统计方法而在 interpretation——R2\n    要求更清晰的 mechanism attribution， R1 要求 F1 regime sensitivity discussion。两者都是 rebuttal\n    可回应的。\n\n    '\n- name: DocRED schema compilation (Phase 0 R2)\n  plan_id: P020\n  description: 'DocRED Phase 0 重跑（被 kill，已被 P004 取代）。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: killed\n    superseded_by: P004\n  result_rationale: '实验被终止，不进入论文。Median 档审稿人不会看到此实验。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: N/A — killed experiment, no paper impact.\n","numLines":712,"startLine":1,"totalLines":712}}}
